      "characters": 1040,
      "text": "Biden, J (2023, March 1). Statement from President Joe Biden on Action to Lower Insulin Costs. The White house \n\nConstantino, A. K. (2023, July 13). Uninsured Americans pay high costs for insulin Eli Lilly vowed to price at $25, Sen. Warren says. CNBC.\n\nEli Lilly and Company. (2023, March 1). Lilly cuts insulin prices by 70% and caps patient insulin out-of-pocket costs at $35 per month.\n\nEli Lilly and Company. (n.d.). About Eli Lilly and Company. \nlast accessed on Feb 4th\n\nhttps://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_Lilly_and_Company\n\nGilbert D . Gregg A. (2023, March 1). Eli Lilly to cut insulin prices by 70 percent. The Washington Post.\n\nLemon, D. (2023, March 1). CEO of pharma giant on why the company is cutting cost of insulin. CNN Business.\n\nSingman, B. (2023, March 1). White House: Eli Lilly’s insulin price cap shows why GOP should stop attacking the Inflation Reduction Act. Fox News.\n\nWikipedia contributors. (n.d.). Eli Lilly and Company. Wikipedia. \nlast accessed on Jan 20th\n\nhttps://www.lilly.com/about/leadership/david-ricks\n"
